      "text": "Move To... This element is a more accessible alternative to drag & drop reordering. Press Enter or Space to move this question. Question 1 1 / 1 pts Edit this Question Delete this Question 0 multiple_choice_question 111098108 <div class=\"tex2jax_ignore\"> <p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Consider the system pictured: a bullet is shot through two holes in disks a distance D apart, attached to a shaft that rotates at constant angular speed with a period T. ϴ describes the fixed angular separation of the holes.</span></p> <p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">For the formula for the bullet speed v in terms of the given variables, would you expect to find D in the numerator or denominator?</span></p> <p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Explain. Be sure to include your explanation in the last question where you show work for this assignment.</span></p> <p><img class=\"display\" src=\"https://d1py7umku9kunm.cloudfront.net/assets/9153772/bulletCylinder_2.JPG\"></p> </div><p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">The angular velocity of a spinning disk is given by ω(t) = A - B t<sup>2</sup>. <span>Through what angle does the disk turn between t</span><sub>0</sub><span>&nbsp;= 0.0s and the time at which it reverses its direction of rotation?</span></span></p> <p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span>Consider the case where A = 18 s<sup>-1</sup>&nbsp;and B = 0.50 s<sup>-3</sup>.</span></span></p> <p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Enter your answer in radians.</span></p> Consider the system pictured: a bullet is shot through two holes in disks a distance D apart, attached to a shaft that rotates at constant angular speed with a period T. ϴ describes the fixed angular separation of the holes. For the formula for the bullet speed v in terms of the given variables, would you expect to find D in the numerator or denominator? Explain. Be sure to include your explanation in the last question where you show work for this assignment. The angular velocity of a spinning disk is given by ω(t) = A - B t2. Through what angle does the disk turn between t0 = 0.0s and the time at which it reverses its direction of rotation? Consider the case where A = 18 s-1 and B = 0.50 s-3. Enter your answer in radians. 2272 numerator numerator exact_answer none 59026256 2272 margin of error +/- 7206 denominator denominator exact_answer none 59026256 7206 margin of error +/- 9950 neither neither exact_answer none 59026256 9950 margin of error +/-"
